+      "content": "You know the *indefinido* from A2 Unit 11, the *imperfecto* from A2 Unit 21 and the contrast between them from A2 Unit 22. At B2 that contrast becomes a storytelling tool. The *indefinido* looks at an action as finished, a closed block, so a chain of *indefinido* verbs forms the plot: first this happened, then that. The *imperfecto* looks at an action from the inside, with no start or end in view, so it suits whatever was already there when the events happened: the time, the weather, a feeling, what someone was doing. Take the *imperfecto* lines out of a story and the plot still moves, but it feels bare."
